ed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:fc00d67b691f819d4cbceb41e67939c316e720731cac53230ccca83096310336","file":"preprints/An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":13,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"0f61cd5379591dfe75c47ec700c41f92e7fae049fc3efbb20dfc17d18d511812","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:fc00d67b691f819d4cbceb41e67939c316e720731cac53230ccca83096310336","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L13"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is one uniform randomized algorithm that, given $x,y$ and a rational\n$\\varepsilon\\in(0,1)$, returns a nonnegative integer $\\widehat D$ such that\n\\[\n \\Pr\\bigl[\\ED(x,y)\\le \\widehat D\\le(1+\\varepsilon)\\ED(x,y)\\bigr]\n \\ge \\frac23.\n\\]\nFor every fixed rational $\\varepsilon$, its worst-case expected running time\non strings of total length $N$ is $N^{1+o(1)}$ as $N\\to\\infty$ on the\nlogarithmic-word RAM. The expectation is over internal randomness only,\nand the bound includes input processing, preprocessing, numerical work,\nrandom sampling and all data-structure operations. Equal strings return zero\ndeterministically."}
